WEBVTT

00:00.375 --> 00:02.044
Hello!

00:05.047 --> 00:08.007
Nice to meet you.
I'm Makoto Tsukauchi.

00:08.008 --> 00:10.761
Koichi and I are dating.

00:11.637 --> 00:13.555
Thanks a lot, Makoto.

00:13.972 --> 00:15.557
Sorry to ask for a weird favor.

00:16.600 --> 00:18.310
It's going to cost you.

00:21.688 --> 00:25.024
Koichi and I go to the same
college, but we're in different years.

00:25.025 --> 00:29.028
My, my. What a lovely
young lady you are.

00:29.029 --> 00:29.278
Koichi!

00:29.279 --> 00:30.488
QUIRK: FLY SWATTER - Koichi!

00:30.489 --> 00:30.530
Koichi!

00:30.531 --> 00:33.199
There you go, showing
off like a fool again!

00:33.200 --> 00:37.411
An attractive girl like her would
never give you the time of day!

00:37.412 --> 00:39.164
You saw through it already!

00:39.540 --> 00:41.625
And for a mean reason, too!

02:13.091 --> 02:14.258
PROFESSIONAL

02:14.259 --> 02:18.971
PROFESSIONAL A PERSON ENGAGED IN A SPECIFIED ACTIVITY
AS A MAIN OCCUPATION RATHER THAN AS A PASTIME

02:18.972 --> 02:20.139
PROFESSIONAL A PERSON ENGAGED IN A SPECIFIED ACTIVITY AS
A MAIN OCCUPATION RATHER THAN AS A PASTIME MOM DESCENDS!

02:20.140 --> 02:21.141
MOM DESCENDS!

02:22.267 --> 02:25.771
In light of this, I can't trust you
about school or anything else either.

02:26.021 --> 02:28.481
I guess I'm going to have
to take you back home.

02:28.482 --> 02:30.274
Anything but that!

02:30.275 --> 02:34.112
Ma'am, I've been keeping
an eye on Koichi's studies.

02:34.446 --> 02:39.159
Besides, I haven't ruled out the
possibility of dating him in the future.

02:39.576 --> 02:45.623
I can't say I think much of using empty
promises to get a person's hopes up.

02:45.624 --> 02:49.085
However, I do like how
well-spoken you are.

02:49.086 --> 02:51.671
Why not really
marry into our family?

02:51.672 --> 02:53.340
I'll consider it.

02:56.510 --> 03:00.721
Um, h-h-h-hello...

03:00.722 --> 03:02.432
Huh? What's up?

03:03.892 --> 03:04.475
I'm leaving!

03:04.476 --> 03:05.644
Whoa, hang on!

03:06.019 --> 03:08.479
Things could go
either way at this point.

03:08.480 --> 03:11.858
I'd at least like to make her
think I'm as popular as possible.

03:11.859 --> 03:15.904
Don't you see that this side of
you is the cause of all this trouble?

03:16.738 --> 03:19.991
So, Mom. This girl is Po—

03:19.992 --> 03:22.035
My name is Kazuho Haneyama!

03:22.327 --> 03:25.496
Oh, your real name's Kazuho.

03:25.497 --> 03:26.706
That's a nice surprise.

03:26.707 --> 03:29.000
Just roll with it, okay?

03:29.001 --> 03:34.297
Um, she lives nearby...
and she hangs out here a lot.

03:34.298 --> 03:35.047
He's such a bad liar.

03:35.048 --> 03:36.340
- He's such a bad liar.
- Um...

03:36.341 --> 03:36.632
Um...

03:36.633 --> 03:39.427
Why would a neighborhood
girl hang out at your place?

03:39.428 --> 03:41.929
I'm curious too.
What's your connection?

03:41.930 --> 03:44.099
C-Connection?

03:44.933 --> 03:46.059
Hey, it's me.

03:46.476 --> 03:49.730
Crap! He'll be the
hardest to explain!

03:50.689 --> 03:53.358
Oh, you've got visitors?

03:53.984 --> 03:54.776
Huh?

03:55.944 --> 03:57.778
Oh, he's handsome.

03:57.779 --> 04:02.367
Stop that. You're young.
Go find a man your own age.

04:03.243 --> 04:06.412
Master, you're dressed
really nicely today.

04:06.413 --> 04:09.499
Yeah, I came straight
here from somewhere else.

04:09.917 --> 04:13.295
Oh, this is my mother,
and one of my schoolmates.

04:20.427 --> 04:21.678
Nice to meet you.

04:21.970 --> 04:23.429
My name is Kuroiwa.

04:23.430 --> 04:25.890
Oh, thank you
for being so polite.

04:25.891 --> 04:27.350
A business card...

04:27.351 --> 04:30.353
And he's got a
name, too: "Kuroiwa."

04:30.354 --> 04:32.605
Of course he has a name.

04:32.606 --> 04:35.983
May I have a business
card too? Networking is key.

04:35.984 --> 04:37.276
LET'S MAKE EACH OTHER'S LIVES NICER CIVIL ASSISTANCE:
NARUHATA AREA REPRESENTATIVE TAKESHI KUROIWA

04:37.277 --> 04:39.947
LET'S MAKE EACH OTHER'S LIVES NICER CIVIL ASSISTANCE: NARUHATA
AREA REPRESENTATIVE TAKESHI KUROIWA - Ah, a nonprofit.

04:40.322 --> 04:42.949
What sort of work do you do?

04:42.950 --> 04:45.952
We support areas where it's
difficult for local governments

04:45.953 --> 04:48.120
or neighborhood
associations to do their work.

04:48.121 --> 04:50.290
Such as here in East Naruhata.

04:50.791 --> 04:55.378
What that means is, we get help from
volunteers like these two youngsters,

04:55.379 --> 04:59.131
and perform tasks like community
cleanup and neighborhood patrol.

04:59.132 --> 05:02.176
Wow, this actually
sounds believable.

05:02.177 --> 05:05.596
But this whole organization
thing must be fake.

05:05.597 --> 05:09.934
Yes, yes. My boy's always
enjoyed doing such things.

05:09.935 --> 05:13.604
He'd go around outside picking up
trash, even without being asked to.

05:13.605 --> 05:15.607
His enthusiasm is a big help.

05:16.108 --> 05:20.528
And so, we typically use
his place here for meetings.

05:20.529 --> 05:25.408
I also use this building's rooftop to
teach basic self-defense techniques.

05:25.409 --> 05:28.369
Ah! That's why he
called you "Master"!

05:28.370 --> 05:31.122
You do look strong, I must say!

05:31.123 --> 05:36.169
You're in amazing shape! Were
you once in some special line of work?

05:36.170 --> 05:38.504
Like the military,
or the police?

05:38.505 --> 05:39.839
She's into muscles?

05:39.840 --> 05:40.923
Gross.

05:40.924 --> 05:42.301
Or maybe...

05:42.718 --> 05:44.803
you were a hero?

05:46.763 --> 05:49.974
Oh, Makoto. Never mind
that whole hero business.

05:49.975 --> 05:51.935
It's best for people
to be ordinary.

05:52.311 --> 05:55.646
All those heroes live
at the whims of others.

05:55.647 --> 05:58.817
I'm sure they must badly
neglect their own lives.

06:00.986 --> 06:03.487
I am here!

06:03.488 --> 06:07.783
My Koichi was eager to
become a hero when he was little.

06:07.784 --> 06:10.077
But maybe he went
about it the wrong way.

06:10.078 --> 06:14.332
He would imitate All Might, poke
his nose into fights and get hurt,

06:14.333 --> 06:17.085
and put himself in danger
trying to help other people.

06:17.461 --> 06:20.838
When it came time for
high school entrance exams,

06:20.839 --> 06:22.757
he went to Tokyo saying
he'd become a hero,

06:22.758 --> 06:25.968
then somehow fell into a
river and failed his exam.

06:25.969 --> 06:31.683
I've never been sure whether to
describe him as "unreliable" or "unsafe."

06:33.227 --> 06:35.229
Th-That's not true!

06:39.483 --> 06:42.151
Kazuho, do you have
an opinion to offer?

06:42.152 --> 06:43.778
I'd like to hear it.

06:43.779 --> 06:45.531
N-Not really.

06:46.990 --> 06:48.909
If you have something
to say, say it!

06:50.494 --> 06:52.746
Oh, she ran off.

06:53.330 --> 06:55.498
Whoops, now I've done it.

06:55.499 --> 06:58.501
I guess I shouldn't hound a
girl I just met with questions.

06:58.502 --> 07:01.587
You didn't question
her. You shouted at her.

07:01.588 --> 07:03.089
Well, don't just stand
here! Go after her!

07:03.090 --> 07:03.756
- Well, don't just stand here! Go after her!
- Ow!

07:03.757 --> 07:04.299
Well, don't just stand
here! Go after her!

07:04.591 --> 07:07.844
Um, what do I do
once I've caught up?

07:07.845 --> 07:10.305
What, indeed?

07:10.848 --> 07:14.726
She made an effort to
look nice. Compliment her.

07:24.361 --> 07:25.404
Got you!

07:28.907 --> 07:32.243
You really are clumsy
when it comes to walking.

07:32.244 --> 07:35.372
I'm going home now!
What did you want?

07:35.873 --> 07:38.750
Well, nothing in particular.

07:39.168 --> 07:40.460
Compliment her.

07:41.420 --> 07:46.425
I just thought, you kind of
look different than usual today.

07:48.760 --> 07:50.261
Oh yeah?

07:50.262 --> 07:53.431
I figured I'd go for
a change of pace.

07:53.432 --> 07:57.978
Um, yeah. It's like...

07:59.396 --> 08:00.606
Like what?

08:01.190 --> 08:03.150
Just say it already.

08:07.446 --> 08:08.697
It's like...

08:10.782 --> 08:12.534
you put that
together in a hurry.

08:14.453 --> 08:17.414
A h-hurry?

08:22.503 --> 08:24.922
So I was in a hurry, so what!

08:27.049 --> 08:28.926
But it was a compliment.

08:40.312 --> 08:42.480
This is such fun!

08:42.481 --> 08:46.234
It's worth visiting the busy
city every now and then!

08:46.235 --> 08:48.778
Just so long as
you're enjoying this.

08:48.779 --> 08:50.571
Koichi, are you okay?

08:50.572 --> 08:53.366
You're making a face
like a Buddha statue.

08:53.367 --> 08:54.575
I am fine.

08:54.576 --> 08:58.371
Keep your mind calm and wait,
and the storm will eventually pass.

08:58.372 --> 08:59.747
My father taught me that.

08:59.748 --> 09:00.289
DETACHMENT - My
father taught me that.

09:00.290 --> 09:01.041
DETACHMENT

09:01.834 --> 09:04.794
AKAKI RICE CRACKERS - Oh yes, I almost forgot.
I need to buy a souvenir for your father.

09:04.795 --> 09:05.879
Oh yes, I almost forgot. I need
to buy a souvenir for your father.

09:09.258 --> 09:09.465
THUNDER GATE

09:09.466 --> 09:11.008
THUNDER GATE - It's an Asakusa
Thunder Gate-exclusive All Might hoodie!

09:11.009 --> 09:12.468
THUNDER GATE MATERIALISTIC DESIRE - It's an
Asakusa Thunder Gate-exclusive All Might hoodie!

09:12.469 --> 09:12.718
THUNDER GATE
MATERIALISTIC DESIRE

09:12.719 --> 09:16.264
You're going to waste money
on another silly thing like that?!

09:16.265 --> 09:17.223
Ow!

09:17.224 --> 09:18.976
I'm just looking!

09:19.393 --> 09:22.228
Ma'am, it's time to
get back on the bus.

09:22.229 --> 09:23.230
Oh, is it?

09:23.480 --> 09:26.274
What would I do without
you here, Makoto?

09:26.275 --> 09:29.403
Or so I said, but I'm
secretly buying one anyway.

09:31.154 --> 09:36.325
This has been Tohato Tours'
Tokyo Sampler half-day tour.

09:36.326 --> 09:40.581
We will now return to our starting point at
Tokyo Station, where the tour will conclude.

09:51.049 --> 09:54.677
Thank you for going
sightseeing with me, Makoto.

09:54.678 --> 09:57.638
You truly are one in a million.

09:57.639 --> 10:00.266
I won't ask you to
marry my son anymore,

10:00.267 --> 10:03.394
but I'd love to trade you for
Koichi so you can be my daughter.

10:03.395 --> 10:07.024
Um, and where
would that leave me?

10:07.399 --> 10:09.025
As a free agent?

10:09.026 --> 10:10.860
You're off the team.

10:10.861 --> 10:12.029
That's mean.

10:33.509 --> 10:35.636
HUTCH THE SOLITARY
BEE - Things might be ready.

10:36.053 --> 10:38.597
Time for a surprise tour.

10:39.056 --> 10:41.058
Let's go!

10:46.688 --> 10:49.399
QUIRK: MONSTER CAT

10:52.819 --> 10:53.570
Ow!

10:55.781 --> 10:56.197
EMERGENCY BRAKE

10:56.198 --> 10:56.990
EMERGENCY BRAKE - Damn it!

10:57.241 --> 10:58.492
It won't stop!

11:02.829 --> 11:04.706
Runaway bus!

11:05.165 --> 11:06.124
Tails!

11:06.667 --> 11:10.128
Hmph, something's
got ahold of that bus.

11:10.504 --> 11:11.797
A cat?

11:12.130 --> 11:15.259
But a cat can't give
me any info on Trigger.

11:15.676 --> 11:17.469
I'll leave this one to the pros.

11:33.277 --> 11:37.197
Hey, old man, don't
call me at weird times.

11:40.117 --> 11:41.660
Huh? Koichi is?!

11:42.911 --> 11:46.123
He's on a runaway
bus? What gives?

11:46.957 --> 11:49.459
It's like he has the worst luck.

11:58.510 --> 12:00.262
Did you bring what I asked for?

12:01.847 --> 12:03.931
A duster and packing tape.

12:03.932 --> 12:05.767
What're you gonna do with these?

12:06.018 --> 12:07.435
We can talk later.

12:07.436 --> 12:09.313
It'll be here soon!

12:24.661 --> 12:26.330
Th-That's...

12:27.080 --> 12:29.875
Turbo Hero:
Ingenium, on the scene!

12:30.292 --> 12:31.418
A cat, huh?

12:38.675 --> 12:40.469
Sorry, I have to
destroy the door!

12:46.934 --> 12:49.018
Is everyone unhurt?!

12:49.019 --> 12:49.853
Oh.

12:53.065 --> 12:55.316
Driver, do you have any control?

12:55.317 --> 12:58.070
No! I can't brake or steer!

12:58.820 --> 13:02.616
This'll be a huge disaster if it goes
charging into the shopping district.

13:09.873 --> 13:11.123
People up ahead!

13:11.124 --> 13:13.794
Master?! What's
that in his hands?

13:14.002 --> 13:15.462
A cat toy?!

13:27.057 --> 13:30.227
Ingenium here. The runaway
bus is now on the expressway.

13:30.477 --> 13:32.019
We see that from here too.

13:32.020 --> 13:37.067
But the road up ahead is closed at
Naruhata due to a ruptured overpass.

13:38.360 --> 13:41.071
Must have been from
that monster incident.

13:42.114 --> 13:45.324
At your present speed, you'll
reach the break in five minutes.

13:45.325 --> 13:49.662
It's convenient that there are no
other vehicles, but there's a time limit.

13:49.663 --> 13:51.790
If this thing jumps, I'd
rather not go down with it.

13:53.250 --> 13:55.210
There you are, Pit-02.

13:55.419 --> 13:58.713
We'll begin transferring passengers
as soon as we're in position.

13:58.714 --> 14:01.465
I don't know why, but the
bus has turned into a cat.

14:01.466 --> 14:02.718
Be careful not to provoke it.

14:03.177 --> 14:04.386
Roger that.

14:04.887 --> 14:08.390
Everyone, we're going to have you
each move to that trailer alongside us!

14:08.682 --> 14:13.353
My staff will receive you, so please
proceed calmly, one at a time, to the exit!

14:13.687 --> 14:14.228
Hey, hey!

14:14.229 --> 14:16.315
ENIGMA - Hey, hey!

14:26.742 --> 14:30.494
Heave-ho. Heave-ho.

14:30.495 --> 14:35.459
Heave-ho. Heave-ho. Heave-ho.

14:36.960 --> 14:38.669
That's everyone?

14:38.670 --> 14:39.670
Yes, sir.

14:39.671 --> 14:40.004
HUTCH THE SOLITARY BEE

14:40.005 --> 14:40.880
HUTCH THE SOLITARY BEE - Well.

14:40.881 --> 14:43.759
That makes it boring, so...

15:05.989 --> 15:07.157
Ow, ow.

15:09.243 --> 15:10.410
Ingenium!

15:11.036 --> 15:12.036
Damn!

15:12.037 --> 15:13.829
Hey, Enigma! You okay?

15:13.830 --> 15:15.332
Heave...

15:18.168 --> 15:19.836
Great! I'm out of fuel!

15:19.837 --> 15:21.547
My speed's dropping!

15:23.257 --> 15:25.049
Ingenium ran out of fuel?

15:25.050 --> 15:28.220
He ran too much while he was
chasing down the bus earlier.

15:28.470 --> 15:29.930
We've got to deliver
some fuel fast.

15:30.556 --> 15:32.391
But Pit-02's out of commission.

15:32.683 --> 15:35.059
Hey, does anyone have
a Mobility-type Quirk?!

15:35.060 --> 15:35.977
- Hey, does anyone have a Mobility-type Quirk?!
- I do!

15:35.978 --> 15:36.353
I do!

15:36.687 --> 15:38.980
I'm the guy who's
pretty fast on his feet!

15:38.981 --> 15:40.565
The Crawler!

15:40.566 --> 15:41.858
You're who, now?

15:41.859 --> 15:43.359
- Stop that, Koichi!
- Ow! Ow!

15:43.360 --> 15:46.946
- Ow! Ow!
- Stay out of this! This is no job for an amateur!

15:46.947 --> 15:46.988
- Ow! Ow!
- Mom! This is no time for that!

15:46.989 --> 15:49.449
Mom! This is no time for that!

15:53.662 --> 15:54.913
Here goes.

15:57.666 --> 15:59.167
Koichi...

15:59.168 --> 16:00.710
Ma'am, are you all right?

16:00.711 --> 16:02.796
- I can help with first aid!
- Oh, Mr. Kuroiwa.

16:06.049 --> 16:07.050
I can't catch up!

16:07.509 --> 16:09.511
That passenger is in danger!

16:09.928 --> 16:11.637
If only I had fuel!

16:11.638 --> 16:13.306
I'm your backup!

16:13.307 --> 16:14.391
Here you go!

16:15.475 --> 16:19.604
You use juice for fuel,
Ingenium? I didn't know that!

16:19.605 --> 16:21.064
You...

16:22.191 --> 16:23.817
What, is it the hoodie?

16:24.234 --> 16:27.528
I'm the guy clad in
Asakusa's history and culture!

16:27.529 --> 16:30.114
The Crawler:
Thunder Gate Special!

16:30.115 --> 16:32.533
No, not that. Why're
you my backup?

16:32.534 --> 16:36.120
Well, they asked me to help
you out after delivering the juice.

16:36.121 --> 16:38.999
True, this was going
to be difficult alone.

16:40.751 --> 16:44.086
We'll just say an ordinary citizen
who happened to be present helped out.

16:44.087 --> 16:44.922
I guess.

16:45.297 --> 16:46.881
I'll handle the hands-on work.

16:46.882 --> 16:49.467
You offer support from
as far away as possible.

16:49.468 --> 16:50.093
Yes, sir!

16:50.344 --> 16:53.262
Be sure to avoid any combat or
dangerous high-speed maneuvers.

16:53.263 --> 16:55.139
Play it safe.

16:55.140 --> 16:55.891
Will do!

16:57.809 --> 16:59.019
All right.

17:00.020 --> 17:01.480
Here goes, partner!

17:04.733 --> 17:06.692
Those tails are a problem.

17:06.693 --> 17:08.904
Crawler! Sorry, I need
you to be a decoy!

17:09.446 --> 17:10.614
Yes, sir!

17:13.617 --> 17:15.076
Hey, hey!

17:15.077 --> 17:17.203
Look at me!

17:17.204 --> 17:18.956
Th-The Cruller?!

17:19.289 --> 17:21.249
I'll keep the villain occupied,

17:21.250 --> 17:25.211
while Ingenium boards the bus
from behind and rescues Makoto!

17:25.212 --> 17:27.256
That's the plan, anyway.

17:30.592 --> 17:31.510
Not good!

17:34.513 --> 17:35.889
Torque over!

17:37.850 --> 17:40.143
Recipro Burst!

17:45.816 --> 17:47.776
Damn! It sped up again!

17:48.026 --> 17:50.194
I'm close to overheating
after that burst!

17:50.195 --> 17:51.238
Now what?!

17:51.488 --> 17:53.114
Two hundred meters
until the broken section.

17:53.115 --> 17:54.574
Ingenium, slow down!

17:54.575 --> 17:56.951
There's no time. Do I use it?!

17:56.952 --> 17:59.454
But if I mess up, I'll
be totally out of action!

17:59.872 --> 18:01.581
I'm going for it!

18:01.582 --> 18:02.331
Wait!

18:02.332 --> 18:03.917
Crawler! It's too dangerous!

18:14.970 --> 18:17.723
Will myself to go faster!

18:19.975 --> 18:22.686
I am here!

18:22.978 --> 18:24.395
The Cruller!

18:24.396 --> 18:25.898
Koichi?!

18:32.070 --> 18:34.865
The runaway bus is
falling through the break.

18:35.741 --> 18:37.074
It's not over yet!

18:37.075 --> 18:38.869
Engine Mod!

18:42.289 --> 18:44.708
Hyper Acceleration!

18:47.377 --> 18:49.379
Rocket Charge!

18:50.631 --> 18:51.839
Crawler!

18:51.840 --> 18:53.049
Jump!

18:53.050 --> 18:54.259
I'll grab you in midair!

18:55.052 --> 18:56.220
Okay!

18:57.095 --> 19:00.682
Ingenium is jumping
across to the opposite side!

19:01.058 --> 19:03.351
I'll use Slide and Glide
on the side of the bus,

19:03.352 --> 19:05.144
and leap to him!

19:05.145 --> 19:06.355
But...

19:06.855 --> 19:09.608
there's not enough momentum!

19:12.277 --> 19:13.819
I'll make up the for the rest...

19:13.820 --> 19:15.155
with force of will!

19:16.740 --> 19:18.283
Accelerate!

19:19.701 --> 19:23.413
He used to be able
to fly, you know.

19:23.747 --> 19:28.501
When he was a baby, he'd float through
the air before he learned to stand up.

19:28.502 --> 19:29.336
Koichi!

19:29.628 --> 19:34.341
I had no idea where he might
fly off to, and I was so worried.

19:35.092 --> 19:38.262
I started using slaps
to make him stop.

19:38.804 --> 19:43.767
But it looks like he's gotten to where
that's not enough to stop him anymore.

19:44.059 --> 19:46.561
No matter how
much parents worry,

19:46.562 --> 19:49.523
there comes a time when
children fly off on their own.

19:50.023 --> 19:55.237
The best we can hope to do
is teach them how to fall safely.

20:01.493 --> 20:02.786
Koichi!

20:04.746 --> 20:05.998
Nailed that landing.

20:06.623 --> 20:10.169
Perhaps you're right about that.

20:22.472 --> 20:25.641
What? You're going
home already, Mom?

20:25.642 --> 20:28.477
You can feel free
to stay longer.

20:28.478 --> 20:28.936
Ow!

20:28.937 --> 20:30.689
Don't say it if
you don't mean it!

20:31.273 --> 20:34.984
Kazuho and Mr. Kuroiwa,
please look after Koichi.

20:34.985 --> 20:37.403
Feel free to hit him if
he does anything bad.

20:37.404 --> 20:38.739
You can count on me.

20:40.199 --> 20:41.782
And you, Makoto.

20:41.783 --> 20:44.744
Things turned out
rather strangely today,

20:44.745 --> 20:47.705
but would you still give
my boy a serious chance?

20:47.706 --> 20:49.999
Mom, you don't give up.

20:50.000 --> 20:52.461
Well, let's see.

20:53.921 --> 20:55.881
I'll keep an open mind about it.

20:56.715 --> 20:59.259
There you go again too, Makoto.

21:11.063 --> 21:12.523
Thirty centimeters.

21:14.233 --> 21:17.151
I figure you can do
fifty, if you practice.

21:17.152 --> 21:19.780
Hopping over low
obstacles could prove useful.

21:22.282 --> 21:24.701
Yeah, but the other day...

21:25.202 --> 21:28.830
I was zooming through
the air! It was cool.

21:29.289 --> 21:31.415
Are you sure you
didn't imagine it?

21:31.416 --> 21:34.878
A sad hallucination
born of a Quirk complex.

21:36.505 --> 21:37.089
No.

21:37.506 --> 21:41.093
It really happened. I
just can't reproduce it.

21:43.262 --> 21:50.519
Maybe that was a one-time miracle
brought about by the power of Asakusa.

21:51.603 --> 21:54.064
I'm not sure I see a connection.

23:25.781 --> 23:28.241
There's an opening event for
Marukane Department Store.

23:28.242 --> 23:31.702
Pop decides to participate
along with some local performers.

23:31.703 --> 23:34.997
Huh? I haven't seen
Master around lately.

23:34.998 --> 23:36.916
Next time, "Event Announcement!"

23:36.917 --> 23:39.753
Things are happening
that I don't know about.
